{#- The incremental fold's one user message. Vars:
      facts — dict from chronicle.scene_facts(): location (str), date (str),
              cast ([str] of "<kind>/<id>" refs). Same head absorb/user.j2
              builds, and for the same reason: the system prompt asks the model
              to say where the scene is and who is present, and the transcript
              does not always contain that. A scene's FIRST location is set
              silently (scenes/moment.py) and cast added before the first
              message is added silently (appearances/transitions.py), so those
              facts appear nowhere in the text — and an incremental fold can
              never recover a fact it was never given.
      prior — the stored summary this refresh folds forward, "" on a
              from-scratch fold (no summary yet, or the covered prefix moved
              under it; see rolling_summary.covered_digest)
      transcript — str (see snippets/transcript.j2): the posts appended since
              `prior` was written when there is a prior, the WHOLE scene when
              there is not. The two cases are labelled differently below so the
              model is never asked to fold new posts onto nothing. -#}
{%- set head = [] -%}
{%- if facts and facts.get("location") -%}{%- set _ = head.append("Location: " ~ facts.location) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if facts and facts.get("date") -%}{%- set _ = head.append("Date: " ~ facts.date) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if facts and facts.get("cast") -%}{%- set _ = head.append("Present: " ~ (facts.cast | join(", "))) -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if head -%}
{{ head | join("\n") }}

{% endif -%}
{%- if prior -%}
Summary so far:
{{ prior }}

Posts since that summary:

{{ transcript }}
{%- else -%}
The scene so far:

{{ transcript }}
{%- endif -%}
